hadiths[72]{hadithnumber,text}:
"13747","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ a lengthy account of the creation of Adam عليه السلام. The narration describes his formation through stages, the passing of Iblis, the breathing of the spirit and the first movement in his sight and nostrils, his sneezing and praising of his Lord, his greeting to a group, and the choice of the Hand and the vision of his progeny, after which the narrator indicated the remainder of the report. > **""Indeed Allah created Adam from dust, then made him clay, then left him until he became altered black mud, then He created him and fashioned him, then left him until he became ringing clay like pottery. Iblis would pass by him and say: thou hast surely been created for a great matter. Then Allah breathed into him of His spirit, and the first thing the spirit reached was his sight and his nostrils, so he sneezed, and he was inspired to praise his Lord, so the Lord said: May thy Lord have mercy upon thee. Then He said: O Adam, go to that company and greet them and see what they say. So he came and greeted them, and they said: upon thee be peace and the mercy of Allah. Then he returned to his Lord, Who asked, though knowing better, what they said. He said: My Lord, when I greeted them they said: upon thee be peace and the mercy of Allah. He said: O Adam, this is thy greeting and the greeting of thy progeny. He said: My Lord, what is my progeny? He said: Choose one of My Hands, O Adam. He said: I choose the Right of my Lord, and both Hands of my Lord are right. So Allah spread His palm, and all that would ever be of his progeny was in the palm of the Most Merciful.""**"
"13748","Abu Musa رضي الله عنه reports in marfu form from the Prophet ﷺ concerning what Adam عليه السلام received when he was brought out of Paradise, including sustenance and knowledge of crafts, and the relation of worldly fruits to those of Paradise. > **""When Allah brought Adam out of Paradise, He provisioned him from the fruits of Paradise and taught him the craft of everything. So these fruits of yours are from the fruits of Paradise, except that these perish while those do not perish.""**"
"13749","Abu Buraydah رضي الله عنه reports in marfu form from the Prophet ﷺ a comparison between the weeping of Dawud عليه السلام and all the people of the earth on one side and the weeping of Adam عليه السلام on the other. > **""If the weeping of Dawud and the weeping of all the people of the earth were weighed against the weeping of Adam, it would not equal it.""**"
"13750","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reports that he asked the Messenger ﷺ whether Adam عليه السلام was a prophet, and the Prophet ﷺ affirmed his prophethood and messengership and that Allah spoke to him directly with the command to dwell in Paradise with his wife. > **""Yes, he was a prophet and a messenger; Allah spoke to him directly. He said to him: O Adam, dwell thou and thy wife in Paradise.""**"
"13751","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ offered to inform of the most excellent in several categories, naming Jibril among angels, Adam among prophets, Friday among days, Ramadan among months, Laylat al-Qadr among nights, and Maryam bint Imran among women. > **""Shall I not inform you of the most excellent of the angels? Jibril. And the most excellent of the prophets is Adam, and the most excellent of days is Friday, and the most excellent of months is the month of Ramadan, and the most excellent of nights is Laylat al-Qadr, and the most excellent of women is Maryam bint Imran.""**"
"13752","Abd al-Rahman ibn Qatadah al-Sulami رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger ﷺ say that Allah created Adam عليه السلام, after which the narrator mentioned the remainder of the report. > **""Allah created Adam.""**"
"13753","Abu Barzah رضي الله عنه reports as an athar concerning Adam عليه السلام after he was cut off from the speech of the angels. He wept at the gate of Paradise for a hundred years, asked why he should not grieve after being sent down without knowing return, was taught three supplications, learned that these were the words by which Allah relented upon him and which would remain for his children, and later instructed his son Hibatullah, known among the people of the Torah and Gospel as Shith, to worship and ask whether he would return to Paradise, whereupon revelation, a sign of a bracelet of Paradise, recognition, prostration, tears, and traces in Hind are described. > **""O Allah, there is no god but Thee alone, without partner. Glory be to Thee, O Allah, and praise be to Thee. My Lord, I have done evil and wronged myself, so forgive me, for Thou art the Most Merciful of the merciful. O Allah, there is no god but Thee alone, without partner. Glory be to Thee, my Lord, I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for Thou art the Most Merciful of the merciful. O Allah, there is no god but Thee, glory be to Thee and praise be to Thee, without partner. My Lord, I have done evil and wronged myself, so forgive me, for Thou art the Oft-Relenting, the Merciful.""**"
"13754","Ubayy ibn Kab رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ described how the angels washed Adam عليه السلام with water and lote leaves, shrouded him, made a lahd for him, buried him, and declared this the practice for the dead of his descendants. > **""The angels washed Adam with water and lote leaves, and shrouded him, and made a lahd for him, and buried him, and they said: This is your practice, O children of Adam, for your dead.""**"
"13755","A variant report states that when Adam عليه السلام died the angels washed him with water an odd number of times, made a lahd for him, and declared it the practice of Adam and his children. > **""When Adam died, the angels washed him with water an odd number of times and made a lahd for him, and they said: This is the practice of Adam and his children.""**"
"13756","Utayy reports that he saw an elder speaking in Madinah, identified as Ubayy ibn Kab رضي الله عنه, who related that when death approached Adam عليه السلام he expressed desire for the fruits of Paradise, his sons went seeking them, met angels carrying shrouds, perfume, axes, spades and baskets, were questioned and told to return because their father had been decreed, returned to find Hawwa recognizing the angels and clinging to Adam, heard Adam bid her leave him to the angels of his Lord, and then the angels seized, washed, shrouded, perfumed, dug, made a lahd, prayed over him, placed him in the grave with bricks, heaped earth, and declared the practice. > **""O sons of Adam, what do you seek and where are you going? Return, for your father has been decreed. Withdraw from me, for I have been afflicted through thee; leave me to the angels of my Lord, blessed and exalted. O sons of Adam, this is your practice.""**"
"13757","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger ﷺ described Idris عليه السلام as a friend of the Angel of Death who asked to be shown Paradise and the Fire, was taken up, saw the Fire in terror nearing unconsciousness while sheltered by the wing, then was shown Paradise and entered it, refused to leave, whereupon it was said to the Angel of Death that he himself had admitted him and that none who enters it shall leave. > **""Hast thou not seen it? Nay, I have never seen anything like today. Where to? To where thou camest. No, by Allah, I shall not leave it after having entered it.""**"
"13758","Aishah رضي الله عنها, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reports that the Messenger ﷺ said that had Allah shown mercy to anyone of the people of Nuh عليه السلام He would have shown it to the mother of the child, then explained the long calling of a thousand years less fifty, the planting and growth of a tree, the construction of the ark amid mockery about running upon land, the gushing of the oven and abundance of water in the streets, and the mother climbing a third, then two thirds, then the top of the mountain with her beloved child until the water overwhelmed them both. > **""If Allah had shown mercy to anyone of the people of Nuh, He would have shown mercy to the mother of the child. Nuh remained among his people a thousand years less fifty, calling them, until at the end of his time he planted a tree which grew great and spread in every direction, then he cut it and began making it into an ark. They would pass by him and ask him, and he would say: I am making it into an ark. So they mocked him and said: He makes an ark on dry land, and how will it run? He said: Ye shall soon know.""**"
"13759","Abu al-Tufayl reports that he asked Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما about the claim that the Prophet ﷺ ran between al-Safa and al-Marwah as a practice, which Ibn Abbas confirmed, then related the command of rites to Ibrahim عليه السلام, the encounter with Satan at the place of running and the race, the journey with Jibril to Jamrat al-Aqabah and the throwing of seven pebbles until he departed, the same at the middle jamrah, the laying down for sacrifice, the white shirt of Ismail, his request for it as a shroud, the attempt to remove it, and the call from behind announcing fulfillment of the vision and the appearance of a white horned ram with large eyes. > **""O Ibrahim, thou hast indeed fulfilled the vision.""**"
"13760","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports that the Messenger ﷺ affirmed that Allah took Ibrahim عليه السلام as a Khalil. > **""Indeed Allah took Ibrahim as a Khalil.""**"
"13761","Samurah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ used to say that on the Day of Resurrection the prophets would be in pairs of mutual close friends apart from the rest, and that among them on that day would be the Khalil of Allah, Ibrahim عليه السلام. > **""Indeed the prophets on the Day of Resurrection, every two of them will be mutual close friends apart from the rest. And a close friend among them on that day is the Khalil of Allah, Ibrahim.""**"
"13762","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that when Ibrahim عليه السلام was taken up he saw a man sinning with a woman and prayed against him so he perished, then saw another man in disobedience and prayed against him, whereupon Allah revealed that he was His servant whose return involved three possibilities of repentance, forgiveness, or righteous offspring from his loins, and reminded Ibrahim that among His Names is al-Sabur. > **""He is My servant, and his return to Me involves three traits: either he repents and I relent upon him, or he seeks My forgiveness and I forgive him, or there emerges from his loins one who worships Me. O Ibrahim, knowest thou not that among My Names is that I am al-Sabur?""**"
"13763","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ described a palace of pearl in Paradise without crack or weakness, prepared by Allah as hospitality for His Khalil Ibrahim عليه السلام. > **""Indeed in Paradise there is a palace of pearl wherein is neither crack nor weakness, which Allah has prepared as hospitality for His Khalil Ibrahim.""**"
"13764","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that he was shown the prophets and that he most resembled Ibrahim عليه السلام. > **""The prophets were shown to me, and I am the most resembling of Ibrahim.""**"
"13765","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the first of creation to be clothed, meaning on the Day of Resurrection, would be Ibrahim عليه السلام. > **""Indeed the first of creation to be clothed is Ibrahim, meaning on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"13766","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said that when Ibrahim عليه السلام was cast into the fire he affirmed the Oneness of Allah in heaven and his own solitary worship on earth. > **""O Allah, Thou art One in heaven, and I am one on earth worshipping Thee.""**"
"13767","Al-Abbas رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Dawud عليه السلام asked by the right of his fathers Ibrahim, Ishaq and Yaqub, and was answered that Ibrahim was cast into fire and patient for His sake, Ishaq offered himself for slaughter and patient for His sake, and Yaqub lost Yusuf, trials which had not befallen the asker. > **""As for Ibrahim, he was cast into the fire and was patient for My sake, and that is a trial which did not reach thee. As for Ishaq, he offered himself to be slaughtered and was patient for My sake, and that is a trial which did not reach thee. As for Yaqub, Yusuf was absent from him, and that is a trial which did not reach thee.""**"
"13768","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports from the Prophet ﷺ in answer to who are the most noble of people that he named Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq, Dhabihullah عليه السلام. > **""Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq, Dhabihullah.""**"
"13769","Abu al-Ahwas reports as a mawquf athar that Asma ibn Kharijah boasted to a man that he was the son of noble elders, whereupon Abdullah رضي الله عنه replied that such description belonged to Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq Dhabihullah ibn Ibrahim Khalilullah عليهم السلام. > **""That is Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq Dhabihullah ibn Ibrahim Khalilullah.""**"
"13770","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that it was asked who is the sayyid, and the Prophet ﷺ named Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim عليهم السلام, then when asked about a sayyid in his ummah described a man given lawful wealth and generosity, who draws the poor near and against whom complaints among people are few. > **""Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. Yea, a man who is given lawful wealth and granted generosity, so he draws the poor near, and his complaints among people are few.""**"
"13771","Al-Abbas, meaning Ibn Abd al-Muttalib رضي الله عنه, reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the one to be sacrificed was Ishaq عليه السلام. > **""The sacrificed one was Ishaq.""**"
"13772","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said Allah gave him choice between forgiveness for half his ummah or his intercession, so he chose intercession hoping it more general, and would have hastened his supplication were it not for the precedence of the righteous servant. When Allah relieved Ishaq عليه السلام from the distress of slaughter, he was told to ask and be given, so he hastened before the assaults of Satan to ask forgiveness for whoever dies associating nothing with Allah and having done good. > **""Indeed Allah gave me choice between forgiving half my ummah or my intercession, so I chose my intercession, and I hope it will be more general for my ummah. Were it not for the precedence of that to which the righteous servant prayed, I would have hastened my supplication. O Allah, whoever dies associating nothing with Thee, having done good, forgive him.""**"
"13773","Abdullah, meaning Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه, reports as a mawquf athar that Yusuf and his mother عليهما السلام were given two thirds of the beauty of people in face, fairness and other traits, such that when a woman came to him he would cover his face fearing she would be tempted. > **""Yusuf and his mother were given two thirds of the beauty of people.""**"
"13774","A further version from al-Tabarani states that Yusuf and his mother were given a third of beauty, which the author notes is apparently a slip, and Allah knows best. > **""Yusuf and his mother were given a third of beauty.""**"
"13775","Anas رضي الله عنه reports as an athar that Yusuf عليه السلام was given half of beauty. > **""Yusuf was given half of beauty.""**"
"13776","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ said Allah conversed privately with Musa عليه السلام in a hundred and forty thousand words over three days, after which Musa found human speech repugnant for what his ears had received of the speech of the Lord. Among that discourse was that none contrive for Him like renunciation of the world, none draw near like restraint from the forbidden, and none worship like weeping from fear of Him. Musa then asked what was prepared and recompensed for them, and was told of Paradise freely dwelt for renunciants, admission without reckoning through shyness and honor for the Godfearing, and the Highest Companionship unshared for those who weep from fear. > **""O Musa, none who contrive for Me have contrived with the like of renunciation of the world, and none who draw near to Me have drawn near with the like of restraint from what I have forbidden them, and none who worship have worshipped with the like of weeping from fear of Me. As for the renunciants of the world, I have permitted them My Paradise to dwell therein wherever they will. As for those restrained from what I forbade them, when the Day of Resurrection comes there shall remain no servant but I shall scrutinize and reckon him except the restrained, for I shall be shy of them and honor them and admit them to Paradise without reckoning. As for those who weep from fear of Me, theirs is the Highest Companionship, unshared therein.""**"
"13777","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said that when Allah spoke to Musa عليه السلام he could see the creeping of ants upon rock on a dark night from a distance of ten farsakhs. > **""When Allah spoke to Musa, he could see the creeping of ants upon rock on a dark night from a distance of ten farsakhs.""**"
"13778","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ instructed him that if asked which of the two terms Musa عليه السلام fulfilled he should say the better, most complete and most dutiful of them, and if asked which of the two women he married he should say the younger, who came saying hire him for he is strong and trustworthy, having seen his strength in lifting a heavy stone from the well and his trustworthiness in bidding her walk behind rather than before him. > **""The better of them and the most complete and the most dutiful. The younger of them, she who came and said: O my father, hire him; indeed the best thou canst hire is the strong, the trustworthy. Walk behind me and do not walk before me.""**"
"13779","Jabir ibn Abdullah رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ was asked which of the two terms Musa عليه السلام fulfilled and answered the more complete of them. > **""The more complete of them.""**"
"13780","Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said it was as if he looked upon Musa عليه السلام in that valley in ihram between two Qatawani cloaks. > **""As if I look upon Musa in this valley, in ihram between two Qatawani cloaks.""**"
"13781","Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports as an athar that the height of Musa عليه السلام was twelve cubits, his staff twelve cubits, his leap twelve cubits, and that he struck Uj ibn Anaq but reached only his ankle. > **""The height of Musa was twelve cubits.""**"
"13782","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports as an athar that when Allah spoke to Musa عليه السلام on the day of al-Tur He spoke with speech other than that with which He spoke on the day He called him, that Musa asked whether this was His speech, was told he was spoken to with the force of ten thousand tongues while His is the force of all tongues and stronger, and that when Musa returned to Banu Israil and was asked to describe the speech of the Most Merciful he declared them unable and likened it only distantly to the sounds of thunderbolts heard in their clearest display. > **""O Musa, I spoke to thee but with the force of ten thousand tongues, and Mine is the force of all tongues and stronger than that.""**"
"13783","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the Angel of Death used to come to people openly, came to Musa عليه السلام who struck him and gouged his eye, returned to his Lord complaining while acknowledging his honor, was sent back to bid him place his hand upon a hide or ox skin with a year for every hair covered, conveyed this, was asked what comes after, answered death, heard that it be now, seized his soul after a scent, and thereafter, his eye having been restored, came to people in concealment. Part of this is noted to be in the Sahih. > **""The Angel of Death used to come to people openly. He came to Musa and he struck him and gouged his eye. Go to My servant and say to him: let him place his hand upon a hide or the skin of an ox, and for every hair covered by his hand there is a year. What is after this? Death. Then now.""**"
"13784","Abu Said رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said he saw Musa عليه السلام at the red dune praying in his grave. > **""I saw Musa at the red dune, praying in his grave.""**"
"13785","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ passed by Musa عليه السلام while he stood praying in his grave. > **""The Prophet passed by Musa while he stood praying in his grave.""**"
"13786","Al-Shabi reports from Jabir ibn Abdullah رضي الله عنهما or another companion of the Messenger ﷺ that the Messenger ﷺ said he would be the first to recover, would raise his head to find a man between him and the Throne, identified as Musa عليه السلام, and that if he had been upon the earth he would have recovered before him. > **""I am the first to recover, so I raise my head, and behold a man between me and the Throne. It is said: This is Musa. If he was upon the earth, he has surely recovered before me.""**"
"13787","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ his hope that if his life be prolonged he would meet Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام, and his instruction that if death hastens him, whoever among his followers meets him should convey his greeting of peace. > **""Indeed I hope, if my life be prolonged, to meet Isa ibn Maryam. If death hastens me, then whoever of you meets him, let him convey my greeting of peace to him.""**"
"13788","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said there is no prophet or messenger between him and Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام except that he is his successor over his ummah after him, that he will kill the Dajjal, break the cross, abolish the jizyah, cause war to lay down its burdens, and that whoever reaches him should convey peace. Part of this is noted to be in the Sahih. > **""Verily Isa ibn Maryam, there is no prophet or messenger between me and him, except that he is my successor over my ummah after me. Verily he will kill the Dajjal, and break the cross, and abolish the jizyah, and war shall lay down its burdens. Whoever of you reaches him, let him convey peace to him.""**"
"13789","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام will descend and remain among people for forty years. > **""Isa ibn Maryam will descend and remain among people for forty years.""**"
"13790","Aws ibn Aws رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام will descend at the white minaret to the east of Damascus. > **""Isa ibn Maryam will descend at the white minaret to the east of Damascus.""**"
"13791","Al-Shabi reports as an athar that a man said before al-Mughirah ibn Shubah رضي الله عنه that blessings be upon Muhammad, the Seal of the Prophets with no prophet after him, whereupon al-Mughirah replied that saying Seal of the Prophets sufficed, for they used to relate that Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام would emerge, and if he emerges then he was both before him and after him. > **""It suffices thee to say: the Seal of the Prophets. We used to relate that Isa ibn Maryam will emerge. If he emerges, then he was indeed before him and after him.""**"
"13792","Abdullah ibn Salam رضي الله عنه reports as an athar that Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام will be buried with the Messenger ﷺ and his two companions رضي الله عنهما, so that his grave will be the fourth. > **""Isa ibn Maryam will be buried with the Messenger of Allah and his two companions, so his grave will be the fourth.""**"
"13793","Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger ﷺ, رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger ﷺ told her that Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام remained among Banu Israil for forty years. > **""Indeed Isa ibn Maryam remained among Banu Israil for forty years.""**"
"13794","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ said thrice that the first to deny was Adam عليه السلام. When Allah created him He wiped his back and brought forth his progeny and presented them, he saw among them a shining man, asked who he was, was told he was his son Dawud, asked his age, was told sixty, asked increase, was told only by giving from his own age, gave forty years, Allah wrote a document with angels as witnesses, and when seizure of his soul was intended he claimed forty remained, was reminded he had given them to Dawud, denied, so Allah produced the document and proof, completing a hundred for Dawud and a thousand for Adam. > **""The first to deny was Adam. When Allah created him He wiped his back and brought forth his progeny and presented them to him. He saw among them a man shining and said: My Lord, who is this? He said: This is thy son Dawud. He said: How long is his age? He said: Sixty. He said: My Lord, increase his age. He said: No, unless thou increasest him from thy age. So he gave him forty years from his age.""**"
"13795","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that when the Messenger ﷺ mentioned Dawud عليه السلام he would describe him as the most worshipful of mankind. > **""He was the most worshipful of mankind.""**"
"13796","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ described the intense protective jealousy of Dawud the Prophet عليه السلام, whose doors were locked upon his exit until his return, the appearance of a man amid the house on one occasion to the alarm of his wife, the questioning of the stranger who feared neither kings nor veils, the recognition of the Angel of Death and welcome of Allah's command, the wrapping at the place of seizure until sunrise, and the shading by birds at the bidding of Sulayman until the earth darkened, whereupon a wing was withheld, with the Prophet ﷺ demonstrating the gesture and mention of prayer upon him that day. > **""Dawud the Prophet had intense jealousy. When he went out the doors were locked and none entered upon his family until he returned. Who art thou? I am he whom kings do not awe and from whom no veil withholds. Then thou art, by Allah, the Angel of Death. Welcome to the command of Allah. Shade Dawud. Withhold a wing.""**"
"13797","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ told his companions that Allah seized the soul of Dawud عليه السلام from among his companions yet they were neither tempted nor altered, and that the companions of the Messiah عليه السلام remained upon his practice and guidance for two hundred years. > **""Allah indeed seized the soul of Dawud from among his companions, yet they were neither tempted nor altered. And the companions of the Messiah remained upon his practice and guidance for two hundred years.""**"
"13798","Abu Musa رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that the first for whom depilatory paste was prepared and who entered the bathhouse was Sulayman ibn Dawud عليه السلام, who upon feeling its heat and distress lamented the punishment of Allah before lamentation would no longer benefit. > **""The first for whom the depilatory was prepared and who entered the bathhouse was Sulayman ibn Dawud. When he entered it and felt its heat and distress, he said: Alas for the punishment of Allah, alas, alas, before alas avails not.""**"
"13799","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ that Sulayman the Prophet عليه السلام, when standing in his prayer place, would see a tree growing before him, ask its name and purpose, plant it if for planting and record it if for remedy, until one day a tree named al-Khar nub declared itself for the ruin of that House, whereupon Sulayman prayed that his death be hidden from the jinn so men would know they know not the unseen, carved a staff to lean upon, which termites consumed until he fell, the extent of eating estimated over a year while the jinn labored, thus making clear to men that had they known the unseen they would not have remained in humiliating punishment. Ibn Abbas would recite it thus, and the jinn thanked the termite by bringing it water wherever it was. > **""What is thy name? Al-Khar nub. For what art thou? For the ruin of this House. O Allah, conceal my death from the jinn until men know that the jinn know not the unseen.""**"
"13800","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ described the trial of Allah's Prophet Ayyub عليه السلام for eighteen years, abandonment by near and far except two close brethren who visited morning and evening, the suspicion of an unparalleled sin voiced by one and conveyed to him, his reply that he knew not but that Allah knew he would pass two disputants mentioning Allah and return home to expiate for them lest Allah be mentioned except in truth, his going out for his need aided by his wife, the delay, the revelation to strike with his foot for a cool bath and drink, her astonished address upon seeing him restored at his best, his affirmation of identity, and the two threshing floors of wheat and barley filled to overflow with gold and silver from two clouds. > **""Indeed Allah's Prophet Ayyub remained in his trial for eighteen years. His kin and strangers abandoned him except two men of his brethren. Strike with thy foot; this is a cool bath and drink. I am he.""**"
"13801","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that he sat in a circle in the mosque discussing the virtues of the prophets and who was most excellent, mentioning Nuh and his long worship, Ibrahim the Khalil of the Most Merciful, Musa the one spoken to by Allah, Isa ibn Maryam, and the Messenger ﷺ, until the Messenger ﷺ came out and asked what they discussed, was told and asked whom they preferred, was told they had preferred him as sent to all mankind, forgiven past and future, and Seal of the Prophets, whereupon he declared none should be better than Yahya ibn Zakariyya, citing his description in the Quran from the command to take the Book with force through Hayya and as confirmer of a Word from Allah, a chief, chaste and prophet righteous, who never did evil nor intended it. > **""What are you discussing among yourselves? Whom have you preferred? None should be better than Yahya ibn Zakariyya. Hast thou not heard how He described him in the Quran: O Yahya, take the Book with force, and We gave him wisdom as a child. He never did an evil deed nor intended it.""**"
"13802","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ said every one of the children of Adam has erred or intended a fault except Yahya ibn Zakariyya عليه السلام, with the addition that he neither intended it nor did it. > **""There is none of the children of Adam but has erred or intended a fault, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya. He neither intended it nor did it.""**"
"13803","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ said none should say he is better than Yahya ibn Zakariyya عليه السلام, who never intended a fault, with the narrator thinking the addition that he never did it. > **""It befits none to say: I am better than Yahya ibn Zakariyya. He never intended a fault, nor did it.""**"
"13804","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said every son of Adam will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with a sin for which He may punish or show mercy as He wills, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya عليه السلام, who was a chief, chaste and prophet righteous, whereupon the Prophet ﷺ stooped to a speck upon the earth, took it, and likened his member to it. > **""Every son of Adam will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with a sin, and He may punish him for it if He wills or show him mercy, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya, for he was a chief and chaste and a prophet of the righteous. His member was like this speck.""**"
"13805","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ said none should say he is better with Allah than Yunus ibn Matta عليه السلام. > **""It befits none to say: I am better with Allah than Yunus ibn Matta.""**"
"13806","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ in the mosque and sat, was asked whether he had prayed and bidden to rise and pray, then bidden to seek refuge from the evil of devils of men and jinn, asked about human devils, prayer, fasting, charity and its most excellent form, the first of the prophets, his prophethood and converse, the number of messengers, the prophethood of Adam, and the greatest verse revealed, to which the Prophet ﷺ answered affirmatively and instructively throughout, ending with Ayat al-Kursi. > **""O Abu Dharr, hast thou prayed? Rise and pray. O Abu Dharr, seek refuge with Allah from the evil of the devils of men and jinn. Yes. Prayer is the best placed; who wills may do less and who wills may do more. Fasting is an obligatory sufficiency, and with Allah is increase. Manifold multiples. The effort of one with little, or secrecy to a poor man. Adam. Yes, a prophet spoken to. Three hundred and a dozen-odd, a great multitude. Ayat al-Kursi: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer.""**"
"13807","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that a man asked the Messenger ﷺ whether Adam عليه السلام was a prophet, how many generations between him and Nuh عليه السلام, between Nuh and Ibrahim عليه السلام, and how many messengers there were, to which the Prophet ﷺ answered affirmatively, ten generations, ten generations, and three hundred and thirteen. > **""Yes. Ten generations. Ten generations. Three hundred and thirteen.""**"
"13808","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said Allah sent eight thousand prophets, four thousand to Banu Israil and four thousand to the rest of mankind. > **""Allah sent eight thousand prophets: four thousand to Banu Israil and four thousand to the rest of mankind.""**"
"13809","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger ﷺ said seventy prophets were sheltered in the shade of a sarhah tree, with obscure terms concerning provision and burdens. > **""Seventy prophets were sheltered in the shade of a sarhah tree.""**"
"13810","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ was sent after eight thousand prophets, among them four thousand from Banu Israil. > **""The Prophet of Allah was sent after eight thousand prophets, among them four thousand from Banu Israil.""**"
"13811","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports as a mawquf athar that the prophets were from Banu Israil except ten: Nuh, Hud, Lut, Salih, Shuayb, Ibrahim, Ismail, Ishaq, Isa and Muhammad, peace upon them, and that every prophet has two names except Isa and Yaqub عليهما السلام. > **""The prophets are from Banu Israil except ten: Nuh, Hud, Lut, Salih, Shuayb, Ibrahim, Ismail, Ishaq, Isa and Muhammad. There is no prophet but has two names, except Isa and Yaqub.""**"
"13812","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ said the prophets are alive in their graves, praying. > **""The prophets are alive in their graves, praying.""**"
"13813","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger ﷺ swear by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim that Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام will surely descend as a just leader and equitable judge, will break the cross, kill the swine, reconcile relations, remove hatred, have wealth offered yet none accept it, and that were he to stand upon his grave and call O Muhammad he would surely answer him. Part is noted to be in the Sahih in abridged form. > **""By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, Isa ibn Maryam shall surely descend as a just leader and an equitable judge. He shall surely break the cross, and kill the swine, and reconcile relations, and remove hatred, and wealth shall surely be offered yet none shall accept it. Then if he stood upon my grave and said: O Muhammad, I would surely answer him.""**"
"13814","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger ﷺ say that among his brethren prophets who passed there were eight thousand prophets, then came Isa ibn Maryam عليه السلام, then himself. > **""Among my brethren of the prophets who passed there were eight thousand prophets, then came Isa ibn Maryam, then came I.""**"
"13815","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that he went out with the Messenger ﷺ on one of the nights carrying purification water, when the Prophet ﷺ heard a caller and bade silence, supplicated for aid in what saves from what he was made to fear, remarked would he said its sister, whereupon the man was inspired to add longing of the truthful, then the Prophet ﷺ sent Anas to bid the caller pray for the Messenger's aid in his mission and for his ummah to accept in truth what their Prophet brought, an exchange over who sent him followed without prior permission, then identification as messenger of the Messenger of Allah, welcome, declaration that the caller was al-Khidr conveying peace and glad tidings of superiority over prophets as Ramadan over months and of his ummah over nations as Friday over days, and upon turning Anas heard him pray to be made of that merciful guided oft-relenting ummah. > **""O Anas, hush. Would he said its sister. O Anas, lay down the purification water and go to this caller, and tell him to pray for the Messenger of Allah that He aid him in that with which He sent him, and to pray for his ummah that they take in truth what their Prophet brought them. I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. Al-Khidr conveys peace to thee and says to thee: Allah has favored thee over the prophets as He favored the month of Ramadan over all other months, and He has favored thy ummah over nations as He favored Friday over all other days. O Allah, make me of this merciful, guided, oft-relented-upon ummah.""**"
"13816","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger ﷺ offered to relate about al-Khidr عليه السلام, then described his walking in the market of Banu Israil, the request of a contracted slave for charity, the declaration of belief and lack, the adjuration by the Face of Allah and hope in his generosity, the offer to be taken and sold rather than disappoint by the Face of the Lord, the sale for four hundred dirhams, the long sojourn unused, the request for work despite age and weakness, the transfer of stones in an hour requiring six men a day, the entrustment of family during travel, the making of bricks until return and the erected building, the adjuration as to his path and affair, the revelation of identity and lesson that whoever asked by the Face of Allah and rejects while able shall stand fleshless with rattling bones, the apology, pardon, offer of family and wealth or freedom, the choice of freedom for worship, and the praise of Allah Who bound and then saved. > **""Shall I not relate to you about al-Khidr? I believe in Allah; what Allah wills of a matter comes to be; I have nothing to give thee. I ask thee by the Face of Allah to give me charity, for I see generosity in thy face and hope for blessing with thee. I believe in Allah; I have nothing to give thee except that thou take me and sell me. Sell me by the Face of my Lord. Whoever is asked by the Face of Allah and rejects his asker while able shall stand on the Day of Resurrection as skin without flesh, bone rattling. Praise be to Allah Who bound me in servitude and then saved me therefrom.""**"
"13817","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports as a mawquf athar that a man of Banu Abs called Khalid ibn Sinan told his people he would extinguish the fire of the two Harras, was challenged by Ammarah ibn Ziyad of his people, went with a company to where it issued from a mountain cleft in a Harrah called Harrat Ashja, drew a line and seated them with instruction not to call him by name if delayed, faced the eruption like reddish horses following one another striking with his staff and chanting his verses until he entered the cleft with it and delayed, was called by name despite prohibition and emerged holding his head declaring they had killed him, instructed burial and exhumation upon passage of donkeys including a dock-tailed one to be found alive, was denied exhumation by Ammarah lest Mudar speak of exhuming the dead, had told of two tablets in his wife's baggage for difficult matters untouched by a menstruating woman, which were handled in menstruation so their knowledge vanished, while his son came to the Prophet ﷺ who welcomed him as son of his brother. > **""I shall extinguish for you the fire of the two Harras. If I delay from you, do not call me by my name. Did I not forbid you to call me by my name? By Allah, you have killed me, so bury me. When the donkeys pass by you, among them a dock-tailed donkey, then exhume me, for you shall find me alive. Welcome to the son of my brother.""**"
"13818","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that Khalid ibn Sinan was mentioned before the Prophet ﷺ, who said he was a prophet neglected by his people, while another version adds that his daughter came to the Prophet ﷺ who spread his garment for her. The report is noted to conflict with the Sahih statement of closest kinship to Isa ibn Maryam as paternal brethren with no prophet between them, and to have been related by al-Thawri from Salim from Said ibn Jubayr as mursal. > **""That is a prophet neglected by his people.""**"
